  "description": "Leggero frameset selected for Cycling Weekly Editor’s Choice list.The Leggero Disc was developed to be fast, light, and stop on demand. Designed alongside our race-proven Leggero with aero profiled carbon, the frameset features bolt-thru axles on the front and rear for improved stiffness and optimal ride quality. The wind-slicing, droplet-shaped tubes are constructed with our top-of-the-line, nano carbon technology, that creates a responsive ride from the gun. Developed with pro riders for over a decade our Leggero has been constantly refined to remain as competitive as possible, the Leggero Disc was the first bike to win a UCI level race in Britain. After countless hours of feedback and testing, the new disc-ready Leggero has emerged. With oversized square stays. The Leggero Disc will be at home on a group ride, tackling climbs or sprinting for the finish line under riders as powerful as Ed Clancy. Tapered head tubeThe tapered head tube significantly improves front end stiffness and creates a stable base for quick handling.Aerodynamic profiling Our most sophisticated carbon fibre is shape into a Kamm-tail tube. The Kamm-tail tube and seat post creates an improved aerodynamic flow, saving precious rider watts.Nano carbonConstruction using nano particles requires less resin, resulting in an overall frame weight reduction. Learn more about Nano carbon technology.",
